WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.240
There are a lot of moving parts with

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:10.560
these elections, and it all adds to the

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.400
political intrigue. The main races are

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.840
for President and Vice President.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.600
But it works a bit differently from

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.159
other countries because the votes are

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.920
separate. So candidates can stand

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:22.400
together as a team, but they don't have

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.040
to. And they may not even end up in power

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.880
together anyway. 

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.520
There are

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.680
congressional elections happening too

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.759
and President Duterte is running for a

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.159
seat in the senate. It's a way for him to

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:40.560
stay in politics, because his six-year

00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:42.479
presidential term is up and he can't run

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.920
again.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:45.840
Now when it comes to the race for

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.479
president, right now there are really

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:51.280
four main candidates.

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:55.439
First up, Ferdinand Marcos Jr who also

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:57.200
goes by the nickname "Bongbong."

00:01:55.439 --> 00:01:59.280
He's the son of the late dictator

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.680
Ferdinand Marcos, and one of the front

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.680
runners.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.280
Manny pacquiao, the world famous boxer is

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.920
also in the ring. He's been a senator

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:24.080
since 2016, but this time he's up for the

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.400
top job and is promising to fight

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.400
corruption. 

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:38.100
Then

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:43.620
there's Isko Moreno.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:49.120
He's a former teen idol who's now Mayor

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:52.319
of the capital, Manila and a self-styled

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.160
centrist. And he hasn't lost his moves.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:06.959
Isko Moreno is very active on social media. He

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:09.840
dispenses medical advice and medical

00:03:06.959 --> 00:03:12.720
stories in his youtube account. And

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.879
finally, Leni Robredo.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:17.200
She's the current Vice President but has

00:03:14.879 --> 00:03:19.360
been sidelined by Duterte.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.000
And in this election she's actually seen

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:23.680
as the main opposition candidate. She's

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.440
been pushing for human rights and is

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.200
someone who would signify political

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:30.159
change if she won.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.840
But that's a big if. Because in the past

00:03:30.159 --> 00:03:34.400
that platform hasn't been very

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.480
successful. 

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:48.000
But here's one

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:51.120
big twist. The current president's

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:53.439
daughter is also part of the story. Sara

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.920
Duterte-Carpio is the Mayor of Davao

00:03:53.439 --> 00:03:58.000
city. At one point the polls had her as

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:00.319
the favorite to replace her father, and

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.720
many expected her to run for president.

00:04:00.319 --> 00:04:05.439
But she didn't. Sara decided to run for

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.519
vice president under a different party,

00:04:05.439 --> 00:04:10.480
and she allied herself with "Bongbong"

00:04:07.519 --> 00:04:11.840
Marcos. 

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:22.240
With

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:24.080
Sara Duterte and "Bongbong" Marcos, you've

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.560
got the latest installment of a

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:29.120
long-running political saga. Their

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:31.680
families have swung between supporting

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.840
and opposing each other for decades.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:36.400
All the way back to the 1980s, when

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.720
Rodrigo Duterte's mother was a leading

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:41.120
figure in the revolution that got rid of

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.400
Ferdinand Marcos senior. 

00:04:45.199 --> 00:04:50.080
Now,

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:51.680
for outgoing president Rodrigo Duterte,

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.520
political allies are going to be

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.600
important. And that's another feature of

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:57.840
these elections, because Duterte is

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:01.360
facing investigations for his signature

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:03.919
policy. What he called his 'war on drugs.'

00:05:29.039 --> 00:05:33.759
It was a violent campaign to crack down

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:36.080
on crime, targeting everyone from big

00:05:33.759 --> 00:05:38.400
gangs to drug users.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:39.360
And the police were encouraged to shoot

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.680
to kill.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.440
Official figures show that more than 8,000

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:45.280
people were killed, but the

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:47.440
Philippines Human Rights Commission and

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:51.120
other rights groups say the real number

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:52.880
is much higher - more like 27,000. Because

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.520
it wasn't just the police, it was

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:57.440
vigilante killings too. There are people

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:59.520
in groups inside and outside the

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:02.639
Philippines pushing for accountability

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:04.639
and justice. Including Maria Ressa, the

00:06:02.639 --> 00:06:06.800
journalist who just won the Nobel Peace

00:06:04.639 --> 00:06:08.880
Prize for her work to expose human

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:10.800
rights abuses. As well as the

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:13.120
International Criminal Court which has

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:15.520
launched an investigation. Many people

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:17.280
see Duterte's run for a senate seat as a

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:19.039
way for him to retain political

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:21.840
influence and protect himself. 

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:47.759
Now one thing that

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.840
surprises a lot of people, particularly

00:06:47.759 --> 00:06:52.319
outside the Philippines is that despite

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:54.160
Duterte's 'war on drugs' and all those

00:06:52.319 --> 00:06:57.199
thousands of people killed -

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:59.280
he's still popular. He has a 67%

00:06:57.199 --> 00:07:02.360
satisfaction rate

00:07:16.319 --> 00:07:20.479
And this is relevant when we think about

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:23.039
who's most likely to succeed him.

00:07:20.479 --> 00:07:25.440
It explains why "Bongbong" Marcos is a

00:07:23.039 --> 00:07:27.840
leading contender, because he's seen as

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:31.199
the same type of strong charismatic

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:31.199
leader as the outgoing president. 

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:46.879
"Bongbong" Marcos is playing up the idea that the time

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:49.360
when his father was in power, was a kind

00:07:46.879 --> 00:07:51.599
of golden era that he wants to restore.

00:08:01.199 --> 00:08:05.440
But the era of Marcos

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:08.000
senior was a time of military

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:10.639
dictatorship and martial law. Marked by

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:13.280
corruption, brutality, hardship and the

00:08:10.639 --> 00:08:15.280
extravagance of the Marcos family. You

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:17.680
might have heard of Imelda Marcos, the

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:18.550
former first lady, and her three thousand

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:21.520
pairs of shoes.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:25.440
But here's another twist. The electoral

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:27.759
commission could still bar "Bongbong"

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:29.599
Marcos because of an old conviction for

00:08:27.759 --> 00:08:31.759
tax evasion. 

00:08:34.159 --> 00:08:38.000
Now, winning the presidential popularity

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:40.479
contest is one thing.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:42.800
Another is doing the job. 

00:09:05.519 --> 00:09:09.200
Just how well the

00:09:07.839 --> 00:09:11.200
different candidates fit that

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:13.440
description is of course a matter of

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:14.160
opinion. But there's everything to play

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.399
for.

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:19.839
And most experts agree, the political

00:09:16.399 --> 00:09:23.399
drama is nowhere near over. It's still

00:09:19.839 --> 00:09:23.399
anyone's game

